# LLM-lib

One LLM client for every app in `git/`. It covers local servers (colibri, LM Studio, llama.cpp,
vLLM, SGLang, mlx-lm, KoboldCpp, text-generation-webui, TabbyAPI, LocalAI, Jan, Ollama), hosted
APIs (OpenAI, OpenRouter, Groq, Together, DeepSeek, Mistral, Gemini, xAI, Fireworks, Cerebras, NVIDIA,
Hugging Face) and Anthropic. Calls can be sync or async, with streaming, tools and structured output.
It also handles the local-server chores: loading a model with the right context, unloading it for a
GPU-heavy step, and knowing how many requests the server really runs at once.

It replaces the near-identical `llm` modules in Just-Finish-It, Text-Speech-Voice / TSV-kokoro,
Silly and Stonks / stock-portifolio-ui. See [MIGRATION.md](MIGRATION.md) for what maps to what.

## Install

From a built tarball (`uv run build` writes it to `dist/`):

```sh
uv add /Volumes/apple_local/git/LLM-lib/dist/llm_lib-0.1.0.tar.gz
uv add "llm-lib[anthropic] @ file:///Volumes/apple_local/git/LLM-lib/dist/llm_lib-0.1.0.tar.gz"  # + Claude
```

Or straight from the checkout, editable, while working on both at once:

```sh
uv add --editable /Volumes/apple_local/git/LLM-lib
uv add --editable /Volumes/apple_local/git/LLM-lib --extra anthropic
```

Python ≥ 3.11. The only required dependency is `httpx2`. The `anthropic` extra adds the official SDK.

## Use

```python
from llm_lib import LLM, Settings

llm = LLM(Settings(provider="lmstudio", model="qwen3.8-27b", load_context=65536))

# one (system, user) turn -> text, reasoning removed
text = llm.complete("You label headlines.", "1. KO beats estimates", json_schema=schema)

# a conversation, with tools -> Completion(text, reasoning, tool_calls, finish_reason, usage)
reply = llm.chat(messages, tools=tools, temperature=0.3)
messages.append(reply.to_message())
for call in reply.tool_calls:
    messages.append({"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": call.id, "content": run(call.name, call.args())})

# streaming; a cancel event set from another thread stops it at the next chunk
for event in llm.stream(messages, cancel=stop_event):
    if event.type == "content":
        print(event.text, end="")

# async: achat / acomplete / astream
reply = await llm.achat(messages)
async for event in llm.astream(messages): ...

# raw text completion of a fully formatted prompt (roleplay frontends)
llm.complete_text(prompt, stop=["\nUser:"])
```

Messages and tools are always **OpenAI Chat Completions dicts**; Ollama and Anthropic are
translated at the edge (tool calls, tool results, images as `image_url` data URLs).

Stream events: `content`, `reasoning` (a `reasoning_content` field, an inline `<think>` block, or
Anthropic thinking), `tool_calls` (complete, once), `usage`, `done` (with `finish_reason`).

### Configuration from the environment

```sh
# .env
LLM_PROVIDER=colibri          # or lmstudio, ollama, groq, anthropic, ... (see Providers)
LLM_MODEL=                    # empty: the one model a local server serves
LLM_TEMPERATURE=0.7
```

```python
llm = LLM(Settings.from_env())                         # LLM_PROVIDER, LLM_MODEL, ...
planner = LLM(Settings.from_env(("ARCHITECT", "PLANNER")))  # ARCHITECT_X, else PLANNER_X, else X
llm = LLM(Settings.from_env(env_file="~/git/Text-Speech-Voice/.env"))  # or LLM_ENV_FILE=...
```

| Setting | Variable (older names also read) |
|---|---|
| provider | `LLM_PROVIDER` (`LLM_BACKEND`, `STORY_PROVIDER`) |
| model | `LLM_MODEL` (`MODEL`, `STORY_MODEL`) |
| base_url | `LLM_BASE_URL` (`OPENAI_URL`, `OPENAI_BASE_URL`), else the provider's own URL variable ([Providers](#providers)) |
| api_key | `LLM_API_KEY`, else the provider's own key variable: `COLI_API_KEY`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GROQ_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, … ([Providers](#providers)) |
| temperature, top_p, top_k, min_p | `LLM_TEMPERATURE` (`TEMPERATURE`), `LLM_TOP_P`, `LLM_TOP_K`, `LLM_MIN_P` |
| max_tokens | `LLM_MAX_TOKENS` (`ANTHROPIC_MAX_TOKENS`) |
| frequency_penalty, repetition_penalty | `LLM_FREQUENCY_PENALTY` (`FREQUENCY_PENALTY`), `LLM_REPETITION_PENALTY` |
| context | `LLM_CONTEXT` (`STORY_CONTEXT`, `CONTEXT_SIZE`) — Ollama's `num_ctx` |
| no_think | `LLM_NO_THINK` (`STORY_NO_THINK`) |
| timeout | `LLM_TIMEOUT` (`LLM_REQUEST_TIMEOUT`, `STORY_TIMEOUT`) — seconds to the next chunk |
| load_context, load_args, parallel | `LLM_LOAD_CONTEXT`, `LLM_LOAD_ARGS`, `LLM_PARALLEL` (`STORY_*`) — LM Studio |
| thinking | `LLM_THINKING` — reasoning on/off where the server has a switch (Ollama `think`, colibri `enable_thinking`, vLLM/SGLang/llama.cpp `chat_template_kwargs`) |
| effort | `LLM_EFFORT` (`LLM_REASONING_EFFORT`, `REASONING_EFFORT`) — `reasoning_effort` on OpenAI-protocol servers, `output_config.effort` on Anthropic, `think` levels on Ollama |

### Providers

Every name below is a `provider`. Each default URL can be overridden with `base_url`, `LLM_BASE_URL`,
or the provider's own variable.

**Local servers** (OpenAI protocol unless noted)

| `provider` | Default URL | URL variable | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| `colibri` | `127.0.0.1:8000/v1` | `COLIBRI_BASE_URL` | key `COLI_API_KEY`; see [colibri](#colibri) below |
| `lmstudio` | `127.0.0.1:1234/v1` | `LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL` | `load_context` loads the model before the first request; `unload()` frees the GPU |
| `llamacpp` | `127.0.0.1:8080/v1` | `LLAMACPP_BASE_URL` | slots read from `/props` for parallelism; `thinking` via `chat_template_kwargs` |
| `vllm` | `127.0.0.1:8000/v1` | `VLLM_BASE_URL` | `thinking` via `chat_template_kwargs` |
| `sglang` | `127.0.0.1:30000/v1` | `SGLANG_BASE_URL` | `thinking` via `chat_template_kwargs` |
| `mlx` | `127.0.0.1:8080/v1` | `MLX_BASE_URL` | `mlx_lm.server` |
| `koboldcpp` | `127.0.0.1:5001/v1` | `KOBOLDCPP_BASE_URL` | |
| `textgen` | `127.0.0.1:5000/v1` | `TEXTGEN_BASE_URL` | text-generation-webui (oobabooga) |
| `tabbyapi` | `127.0.0.1:5000/v1` | `TABBY_BASE_URL` | |
| `localai` | `127.0.0.1:8080/v1` | `LOCALAI_BASE_URL` | |
| `jan` | `127.0.0.1:1337/v1` | `JAN_BASE_URL` | |
| `ollama` | `127.0.0.1:11434` | `OLLAMA_HOST` / `OLLAMA_URL` | native `/api/chat`: `num_ctx`, `think`, `format`; `unload()` evicts the model |
| `openai-compatible` | `base_url` required | | anything else that speaks `/v1/chat/completions` |

Local servers that don't check a key get a placeholder one. With no `model` set, a server that
lists exactly one model (colibri, llama.cpp, vLLM, mlx-lm, …) has that one used.

**Hosted APIs** (OpenAI protocol, API key required: creating the client without one raises, naming
the variable)

| `provider` | Key variable | | `provider` | Key variable |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `openai` | `OPENAI_API_KEY` | | `gemini` | `GEMINI_API_KEY` / `GOOGLE_API_KEY` |
| `openrouter` | `OPENROUTER_API_KEY` | | `xai` | `XAI_API_KEY` |
| `groq` | `GROQ_API_KEY` | | `fireworks` | `FIREWORKS_API_KEY` |
| `together` | `TOGETHER_API_KEY` | | `cerebras` | `CEREBRAS_API_KEY` |
| `deepseek` | `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` | | `nvidia` | `NVIDIA_API_KEY` |
| `mistral` | `MISTRAL_API_KEY` | | `huggingface` | `HF_TOKEN` |

`effort` goes out as `reasoning_effort` on all of them. DeepSeek, NVIDIA and Hugging Face get a JSON
schema in the prompt only, since they don't enforce `response_format: json_schema` across their models.

**Other**

| `provider` | Notes |
|---|---|
| `anthropic` | through the SDK; default `claude-opus-5-5`; `fallbacks: "default"` on current models; sampling params dropped where they 400. Point `base_url` at colibri to use its `/v1/messages`. |
| `mock` | canned streamed reply, no server |

Aliases also work, for example `lm studio`, `llama.cpp`, `coli`, `oobabooga`, `kobold`, `mlx-lm`,
`tabby`, `grok`, `google`, `hf`, `nim` and `claude`.

### colibri

`Settings(provider="colibri")` handles what colibri's gateway is strict about:

- **model**: colibri refuses a request whose `model` isn't the id it serves. When none is set, the
  client asks `/v1/models` and uses that one (again on the next request if the server was down).
- **API key**: read from `COLI_API_KEY` / `COLIBRI_API_KEY`. It is only checked when the server runs with one.
- **penalties**: `frequency_penalty`, `presence_penalty` and repetition penalties get a 400 from
  colibri, so they're left out (and logged once). A shared `.env` with `FREQUENCY_PENALTY` keeps working.
- **retries**: a 429 (queue full, or the wait for a slot timed out) is resent after `Retry-After`.
  A 5xx is not, because it may come hours into a generation.
- **thinking**: `thinking=True/False` → `enable_thinking`; `effort` → `reasoning_effort`
  (`thinking=False` with an effort sends `"none"`). Timeouts default to three days.
- **parallelism**: `server_parallel` reads its KV slots from `/health`.
- colibri's own request fields pass straight through as keywords, e.g.
  `llm.chat(msgs, cache_slot=0, strict_tool_calls=True, x_colibri_ignore_leading_stop=True)`.

Its other endpoints are in `llm_lib.servers.colibri`:

```python
from llm_lib.servers.colibri import Colibri, choice, noul, score

col = Colibri.from_settings(settings)        # or Colibri("http://127.0.0.1:8000", api_key="...")
col.health(); col.metrics(); col.model_id()

# System One (POST /v1/systemone): closed questions answered with a probability per option
d = col.decide(ticket, {
    "urgent": noul("Does this message express urgency?"),
    "team": choice("Which team should handle this?", {"billing": "payments", "technical": "bugs"}),
    "severity": score("How severe is the impact?", ["none", "minor", "blocked", "losing money"]),
}, pin_state=True)
d["team"].choice, d["team"].confidence, d["urgent"].noul, d["severity"].level

# Image generation on a colibri serving Qwen-Image (POST /v1/images/generations)
img = col.generate_image("a red fox in the snow", size="1024x576", steps=8, seed=42)
Path("fox.png").write_bytes(img.png)
```

### Built in

- **Picks the model** a single-model server serves when `model` is unset (asked once, and again
  after a request that found the server down).
- **Leaves out fields a server refuses** (colibri's penalties) and logs it once instead of failing.
- **Thinking and effort** reach each server in its own form: `/no_think` (`no_think`), Ollama `think`,
  colibri `enable_thinking`, `chat_template_kwargs`, `reasoning_effort`, Anthropic `output_config.effort`.
  Inline `<think>` blocks come back as `reasoning` events (`strip_think=False` keeps them in the text).
- **Resends a passing 5xx** (`retry_waits`, default 2 s, 5 s, 10 s), e.g. when LM Studio answers
  "Internal Server Error" while it JIT-loads. It also resends a **429** after its `Retry-After`
  (3 times, or 10 for colibri). It never resends a context overflow (`LLMContextExceeded`).
- **Asks for token usage** in streams, and stops asking for good once a server rejects `stream_options` (400 or 422).
- **JSON schema**: enforced where the server supports it. A reply that comes back empty or isn't
  JSON is asked for once more with the schema in the prompt only.
- **Errors**: `LLMUnavailable` / `LLMTimeout` / `LLMCancelled`, `LLMStatusError` / `LLMContextExceeded`,
  `LLMRefusal`. HTML error pages are called out as a server crash. `is_retryable(exc)` is for app-level retry loops.
- **Logging**: `LLM(settings, log=print)` writes `-> LM Studio (qwen): sending request (~1,234 chars)`
  and `<- ... replied in 4.2s (~310 chars)`, with notes like *cut off at the 4,096-token limit*. The
  same lines go to the `llm_lib` logger.

### Extras

```python
from llm_lib import FailoverLLM
llm = FailoverLLM(LLM(main), LLM(backup), primary_off=lambda: video_job_running)

from llm_lib.servers.lmstudio import LMStudio
lms = LMStudio()
lms.models(); lms.loaded_context("qwen"); lms.load("qwen", 65536, parallel=2); lms.unload_all()
with lms.models_unloaded():   # lms CLI: unload all, run the step, reload each exactly as it was
    run_image_model()

from llm_lib.servers.capacity import effective_parallel
workers, why = effective_parallel(4, settings, window=16384)   # LM Studio parallel, llama.cpp / colibri slots, ...

from llm_lib import ThinkFilter, strip_reasoning, extract_json
```

## Layout

```
src/llm_lib/
  client.py        LLM: chat / complete / stream and their async twins, retries, logging
  settings.py      Settings, provider presets, from_env()
  types.py         Request, Event, Completion, ToolCall, Usage
  errors.py        the LLMError hierarchy
  reasoning.py     ThinkFilter, strip_reasoning      jsonutil.py   extract_json, has_json
  failover.py      FailoverLLM                         retry.py      is_retryable, interruptible_sleep
  providers/       openai (SSE), ollama (NDJSON), anthropic (SDK), mock -- wire formats, no I/O
  servers/         lmstudio, colibri, capacity -- talking to the servers themselves
tests/             one file per provider/server, against mocked wire formats
tools/build/       the `uv run build` command (dev only)
```

## Develop

```sh
uv sync
uv run pytest
uv run ruff check
uv run build              # lint + tests, then dist/llm_lib-<version>.tar.gz and .whl, install-checked
uv run build --sdist      # the tarball only (--no-check skips lint/tests, --no-verify the install check)
```

Another app installs a built tarball with `uv add /Volumes/apple_local/git/LLM-lib/dist/llm_lib-0.1.0.tar.gz`.
`build` is a dev-only command (`tools/build`) and isn't installed with the library, so it can't
shadow an app's own `uv run build`.
